## Quick Start

### 1. Local Development

```bash
# Start infrastructure
docker-compose up -d

# Run migrations
make migrate-up

# Build and run
make build
make run-api    # Terminal 1
make run-worker # Terminal 2

# Test CLI
./bin/envsend --help
```

### 2. Send a Secret

```bash
# Create test file
echo "API_KEY=secret123" > test.env

# Send with defaults (10 min, 1 view)
./bin/envsend test.env

# Send with passphrase
./bin/envsend test.env --require-passphrase

# Send for specific recipient
./bin/envsend test.env --ssh github:username
```

### 3. Receive a Secret

```bash
# Receive and decrypt
./bin/envsend receive <url> > received.env

# Verify
cat received.env
```

---

## Production Deployment

### Kubernetes

```bash
# Build and push images
make docker-build
make docker-push

# Deploy to Kubernetes
kubectl apply -f deployments/kubernetes/

# Verify
kubectl get pods -n envsend
kubectl logs -n envsend -l app=envsend-api
```

### Configuration

All configuration via environment variables (see [.env.example](file:///d:/Programs/Next%20js%20%7Bprojects%7D/envsend/.env.example)):
- Database URL
- Redis URL
- MinIO/S3 credentials
- Rate limits
- Expiry defaults

